<title>USA: U.S. Kansas, Texas fed cattle $67, up $1- feedlots.</title>
<headline>U.S. Kansas, Texas fed cattle $67, up $1- feedlots.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. feedlot cattle in Kansas and the Texas Panhandle area sold actively at $67.00 per cwt, up $1 from Tuesday's brisk sales, feedlot sources said.</p>
<p>About 6,000 head sold in Texas and about 5,000 in Kansas, the sources said.</p>
<p>Gains were attributed to talk of strong beef demand following brisk beef sales on Tuesday, albeit at lower prices, they said.</p>
</text>
